| “collect the required resources in the storage and deliver them to the requesting agent in a specified location”       | Goal     | This states the desired mission outcome: resources must end up with the requesting agent at the specified location. It does not, by itself, fully specify every operational detail. |
| “required resources”                                                                                                   | Resource | The resources are physical entities whose availability is central to the mission.                                                                                                   |
| “storage”                                                                                                              | Resource | The storage is a physical place/entity that must be available because it contains the required resources.                                                                           |
| “requesting agent”                                                                                                     | Resource | The requesting agent is an entity involved in the mission, specifically the recipient that must be available/identified for delivery.                                               |
| “specified location”                                                                                                   | Resource | The location is a physical/informational entity required for the delivery to be completed.                                                                                          |
